        "statement": "Let $z$ be a primitive root of odd order $\\ell>1$. Write $N=\\ell N_1+N_0$ for $N\\in\\mathbb Z$ and $r=\\ell r_1+r_0$ for $r\\ge0$, with $0\\le N_0,r_0<\\ell$. The symmetric quantum binomial, interpreted by its Laurent-polynomial product for negative upper index, satisfies\n$$\\begin{bmatrix}N\\\\r\\end{bmatrix}_z=\\binom{N_1}{r_1}\\begin{bmatrix}N_0\\\\r_0\\end{bmatrix}_z.$$\nFor a specialized family $X^{(n)}$ with the divided-power multiplication of [[lem-divided-power-and-toral-quantum-binomial-reordering-identities]],\n$$X^{(a\\ell+r)}=\\frac{(X^{(\\ell)})^aX^r}{a![r]_z!}\\qquad(a\\ge0,\\ 0\\le r<\\ell).$$\nIn particular the family is generated by $X$ and $X^{(\\ell)}$; modulo the ideal generated by $X$, a divided power vanishes unless its index is divisible by $\\ell$, and $X^{(a\\ell)}=(X^{(\\ell)})^a/a!$.",
